2.   See What’s On Your Ballot

# See What’s on Your Ballot

Voters are encouraged to read their County Voter Information Guide to help them be prepared prior to casting their ballots.

![Image 2: A stack of County Voter Information Guides ready to be mailed out](https://files.santaclaracounty.gov/exjcpb1296/styles/card_horizontal_850x478/s3/2023-08/county-voter-information-guides.jpeg.webp?VersionId=R.rXFrlIMZcREy1VAsiXnaYiQUQi__4H&itok=c2a5Icnw)

 A stack of County Voter Information Guides ready to be mailed out 

The County Voter Information Guide (CVIG) is an important tool to help voters prepare for casting their ballots. Voters are encouraged to read it carefully before Election Day and take it with them to the Vote Centers.

The guide contains election resourceful information. It includes voting instructions, a sample of the ballot, candidate statements, measure documents, and other resourceful election information.

With our Preview service, you can now view you sample ballot before you even leave your house. Simply enter your address and our interface will display all the candidates and measures that will appear on your ballot. This service empowers you to make informed decisions on Election Day.

[County Voter Information Guide](https://vote.santaclaracounty.gov/vote-mail/county-voter-information-guide "County Voter Information Guide")

